cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite this Zenodo record and the accompanying manuscript."
title: "PortabilityRisk: occurrence-level portability architecture of acquired antimicrobial resistance determinants across complete bacterial genomes"
abstract: >-
  Occurrence-level computational assignments for 74,349 acquired antimicrobial
  resistance gene occurrences across 6,288 closed complete Gram-negative
  bacterial genomes. Each occurrence is resolved to a documented chromosome or
  plasmid using NCBI molecule designations rather than prediction, and receives
  one of five operational portability classes (A-E) combining documented
  location, plasmid mobilization machinery and chromosomal mobile-element
  context. Homology-based mobile-element proximity and structurally resolved
  complete insertion-sequence detection are recorded as distinct evidence
  levels. No transfer experiment, conjugation phenotype or active transposition
  was measured. Data dictionaries, denominator and evidence-level dictionaries,
  JSON schemas, a provenance map, software and database versions, checksums and
  a standalone verification script are included.
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
